#!/bin/bash
# The WadSpaces Client, the kiosk's shell (etc/sway/wadspaces.conf). Restarted if it
# ever exits, after a pause so a crash can't spin. Its output goes to the
# journal: journalctl -b -t client.
#
# Until the switch there are two: the Tauri app (/usr/bin/client) and the
# native one (/usr/bin/client-native, apps/desktop). A line "native" in
# ~/.config/wadspaces/client runs the native one (read at each start: sign
# out, or reboot, to change).
pick="${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-${HOME}/.config}/wadspaces/client"
while true; do
    bin=/usr/bin/client
    if [[ -x /usr/bin/client-native ]] && grep -qx native "${pick}" 2> /dev/null; then
        bin=/usr/bin/client-native
    fi
    systemd-cat -t client "${bin}" --kiosk
    sleep 2
done
